    "body": "Status of `issue/3450-dxf-classes-section` on the fork `qsmits/Camcraft` (head `41f8b1004`).\n\nA second cause refused the real AC1015 files. When the reader skipped `CLASSES`, the `OBJECTS` reader then refused the file with this text:\n\n```\nDICTIONARY: unsupported dictionary group 102 or value\n```\n\nEach object of the real files has a reactor bracket (`102 {ACAD_REACTORS` .. `102 }`). The `OBJECTS` reader also refused each object type other than `DICTIONARY`. The `OBJECTS` sections of `q04` and `q06` hold these objects:\n- `DICTIONARY` (3)\n- `LAYOUT` (2)\n- `ACDBDICTIONARYWDFLT` (1)\n- `ACDBPLACEHOLDER` (1)\n\nWhat the branch now does:\n- It skips `CLASSES`, `THUMBNAILIMAGE` and `ACDSDATA` to their `ENDSEC` (part 1).\n- It reads a balanced group 102 bracket as opaque data. A broken bracket is a named error.\n- A `DICTIONARY` keeps all its checks from #3176.\n- It reads each other object as an inert record. It takes only the handle and the owner, and adds the object to the ownership graph of #3176. An unowned object, a graphical entity in `OBJECTS` and a missing `ENDSEC` stay named errors.\n- The decision is in `docs/decisions/3450-dxf-classes-section.md`. It says why this keeps what the #3176 decision protects: the reader keeps no object data, and the entity readers stay strict.\n\nReal files, through `dxf::parse` and `SketchData::from_dxf`:\n- `q04-vcarve-sign-letters.dxf`: imports, 300 entities, 2 closed chains.\n- `q04-vcarve-sign-letters-r12.dxf`: imports, 894 entities, 2 closed chains.\n- `q06-die-lines.dxf`: imports, 117 entities, 1 closed chain.\n\nThe pinning tests are in `crates/geometry/tests/dxf_objects_section.rs` (5 pass) and `crates/geometry/tests/dxf_classes_section.rs` (7 pass).\n\nThe work is larger than `effort:medium`: the second cause changed the refusal law of the `OBJECTS` reader. A collaborator must raise the label to `effort:high`.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
